  <!-- ==============================================================
       3C. FREQUENTLY ANSWERED QUESTIONS (Accordion)
       ============================================================== -->
  <section class="faq-section" id="faqSection">
    <div class="container faq-container">
      <div class="section-center-head">
        <span class="faq-kicker">QUESTIONS &amp; TRANSPARENCY</span>
        <h2 class="faq-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <p class="discipline-sub">Direct, transparent answers regarding our calculation engine, empirical methodology, and regulatory compliance.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-accordion-group" id="faqAccordionGroup">
        <!-- Question 1 -->
        <details class="faq-item" open>
          <summary class="faq-summary">
            <span class="faq-question">How does astronomical ephemeris link with financial price action?</span>
            <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">&plus;</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Financial markets are driven by cyclical human psychology: fear, euphoria, liquidity expansion, and risk aversion. For centuries, quantitative researchers from W.D. Gann to modern cyclical analysts observed that celestial movements (planetary cycles, retrogrades, lunations) match recurring macro rhythms.</p>
            <p>We do not treat astrology as mystic fate. We treat it as an astronomical clock &mdash; measuring mathematical cyclical frequencies against 24 years of real tick data from the National Stock Exchange of India (NSE).</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <!-- Question 2 -->
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-summary">
            <span class="faq-question">Is Cosmic Finance SEBI registered or offering buy/sell investment advice?</span>
            <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">&plus;</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p><strong>No.</strong> Cosmic Finance is strictly an educational research and mathematical ephemeris calculation tool. We are not a SEBI-registered investment advisor or research analyst. We never provide buy/sell recommendations, stock tips, target prices, or portfolio management services.</p>
            <p>All data, patterns, and historical statistics are presented strictly for academic research and educational backtesting. Always consult a licensed SEBI-registered financial advisor before risking capital in equity or derivatives markets.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <!-- Question 3 -->
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-summary">
            <span class="faq-question">How accurate are the astronomical calculations on the site?</span>
            <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">&plus;</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Our backend engine calculates true geocentric positions with <span class="mono-num">0.001&deg;</span> arc-second precision using the Lahiri (Chitra Paksha) Ayanamsa. We compute only the traditional Vedic Navagrahas (Sun, Moon, Mars, Mercury, Jupiter, Venus, Saturn, and lunar nodes Rahu & Ketu positioned exactly <span class="mono-num">180.00&deg;</span> apart).</p>
            <p>Positions are cached with high performance on local servers, guaranteeing zero latency when inspecting the 3D celestial sphere or scrubbing the 4D Time Machine.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <!-- Question 4 -->
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary class="faq-summary">
            <span class="faq-question">Can a personal Kundli guarantee profits in trading?</span>
            <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">&plus;</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p><strong>Absolutely not.</strong> No astrological chart guarantees market profits. Trading success requires strict risk management, position sizing, edge validation, and emotional discipline.</p>
            <p>In traditional Vedic astrology, a natal chart highlights psychological predispositions &mdash; such as an individual's inclination toward impulsiveness during malefic dashas, or periods of mental clarity. Our Kundli engine analyzes the 2nd, 5th, 9th, and 11th houses as a self-awareness tool to help you trade with greater discipline, never as a get-rich-quick formula.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
